{"rulings":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-153ec732","decision":"reject","rationale":"The tipping evidence is the current source itself: `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:253-262` no longer compares `bio_large` to `bio_small * 0.95`; it now uses a flat viability threshold (`min_nitrifier_g = 0.02`) and asserts both runs exceed it. A local run of `cargo test -p tank_harness probe_biofilter_scaling_bigger_media_faster_cycling -- --nocapture` passes, so the amendment's central claim that the probe is red because of a 95% biomass-parity assertion is stale. There is still a plausible naming/coverage mismatch because the test no longer directly asserts 'faster cycling,' but that is a different and weaker issue than the specific disputed amendment."}],"summary":"Rejected the disputed amendment because its core factual predicate is outdated: the current test no longer uses the 95% nitrifier-biomass comparison and is not failing on that basis."}